<title>PARAGUAY: SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT ECUADOR 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT ECUADOR 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay beat Ecuador 1-0</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0) in a South American World Cup qualifying match</p>
<p>on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Miguel Benitez (23rd minute)</p>
<p>Attendance: 37,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Colombia     6  4  2  0  12  5 14</p>
<p> Paraguay     5  3  1  1   6  3 10</p>
<p> Ecuador	6  3  0  3   8  7  9</p>
<p> Argentina    5  2  2  1   9  6  8</p>
<p> Uruguay	4  2  0  2   4  5  6</p>
<p> Peru	   5  1  3  1   5  7  6</p>
<p> Bolivia	5  1  2  2   9  7  5</p>
<p> Chile	  4  1  1  2   7  8  4</p>
<p> Venezuela    6  0  1  5   5 17  1</p>
<p>Next match: Nov 12 - Chile v Uruguay</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the World Cup finals.</p>
<p>Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
